IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mwa-types`
IMPORT `mwa-rates`
IMPORT `mwa-payment`
IMPORT `mwa-enforcement`
IMPORT `mwa-goal`

-- Minimum Wage Act 1983 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from ../source/MWA1983.txt, not from the code.
-- The Order below is made up for the tests (an adult rate of $23.15 and
-- three starting-out classes at 80%); the Act fixes no rate of its own.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

`no benefits` MEANS `Benefit history` OF EMPTY, 0

`a day in 2024` MEANS Date 1 7 2024

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Benefit history`
`jobseeker support for` months MEANS `Benefit history` OF (LIST `(da) jobseeker support`), months

-- A worker: age, supervising, training contract, in the Order's training
-- class, benefit history, months with any employer, with any employer since
-- the benefit run, with the current employer.
-- The employment periods are given as months before `a day in 2024`, and
-- turned into first days of work: n months before 1 July 2024 is completed
-- on 30 June 2024.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`started months before` n MEANS `add months` `a day in 2024` (0 MINUS n)

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, supervises IS A BOOLEAN, training IS A BOOLEAN, `training class` IS A BOOLEAN,
      benefits IS A `Benefit history`, `any` IS A NUMBER, since IS A NUMBER, current IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Worker
`worker` age supervises training `training class` benefits `any` since current MEANS
    Worker OF TRUE, age, supervises, training, `training class`, benefits, `started months before` `any`, `started months before` since, `started months before` current, `none of the s 9 classes`, NOTHING

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Worker
`an adult worker aged` age MEANS `worker` age FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 24 24 24

GIVEN w IS A Worker, p IS A Permit
GIVETH A Worker
`with permit` w p MEANS
    Worker OF w's `an employee under s 6 of the Employment Relations Act 2000`, w's `age in years`, w's `involved in supervising or training other workers`,
              w's `employed under a contract of service requiring training for qualification`, w's `in a class the Order defines for the training rate`,
              w's `benefit history`, w's `first day of continuous employment with any employer`,
              w's `first day of continuous employment with any employer since the benefit run`,
              w's `first day of continuous employment with the current employer`, w's `s 9 class`, JUST p

GIVEN w IS A Worker, s IS A `Section 9 class`
GIVETH A Worker
`in s 9 class` w s MEANS
    Worker OF w's `an employee under s 6 of the Employment Relations Act 2000`, w's `age in years`, w's `involved in supervising or training other workers`,
              w's `employed under a contract of service requiring training for qualification`, w's `in a class the Order defines for the training rate`,
              w's `benefit history`, w's `first day of continuous employment with any employer`,
              w's `first day of continuous employment with any employer since the benefit run`,
              w's `first day of continuous employment with the current employer`, s, w's `exemption permit`

`eighty per cent` MEANS `a percentage of the minimum adult rate` 80

-- Class A: ages 16-17, not yet 6 months with the current employer (factor (ii)).
`class A` MEANS `Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`
-- Class B: ages 18-19, 6 months or more on a specified benefit, not yet
-- 6 months with any employer since (factors (i) and (ii)).
`class B` MEANS `Starting-out class` OF 18, 19, JUST 6, JUST `any employer`, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`
-- Class C: ages 16-19 on a training contract (factor (iii)).
`class C` MEANS `Starting-out class` OF 16, 19, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, 6, `eighty per cent`

`the Order` MEANS `Minimum Wage Order` OF 23.15, (LIST `class A`, `class B`, `class C`), JUST `eighty per cent`


GIVEN w IS A Worker
GIVETH A `Rate that governs`
`rate for` w MEANS `the rate that governs` w `under` `the Order` `on` `a day in 2024`

`no board or lodging` MEANS `Board and lodging` OF FALSE, NOTHING, 0, FALSE, NOTHING, 0

GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER, `travel time` IS A NUMBER, b IS A `Board and lodging`, paid IS A NUMBER, lost IS A LIST OF `Time lost`
GIVETH A `Pay period`
`period` hours `travel time` b paid lost MEANS `Pay period` OF `a day in 2024`, hours, lost, `travel time`, b, paid

§§ `Goal 1 — does the Act apply (ss 2, 9)`

#ASSERT `the Act applies to` (`an adult worker aged` 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `(b) an apprentice bound by an indenture of apprenticeship entered into under an Act`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (`(d) an inmate of a charitable institution who does work in or in connection with it` FALSE))
-- s 9(d) "(not being persons residing on the premises by reason only of their being employed therein)"
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (`(d) an inmate of a charitable institution who does work in or in connection with it` TRUE))
-- s 9(e) excludes only the travel, not the employee
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `(e) an employee to whom the Home and Community Support (Payment for Travel Between Clients) Settlement Act 2016 applies`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to` (Worker OF FALSE, 30, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `no benefits`, Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 2020, `none of the s 9 classes`, NOTHING)

§§ `Goal 1 — benefits (s 4A(1)(c)(i), (6))`

#ASSERT `a specified social security benefit` `(da) jobseeker support`
#ASSERT `a specified social security benefit` `(i) youth payment`
#ASSERT NOT `a specified social security benefit` `another payment`
#ASSERT `the continuous social assistance period in months` (`jobseeker support for` 7) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the continuous social assistance period in months` (`Benefit history` OF (LIST `(da) jobseeker support`, `another payment`), 7) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the continuous social assistance period in months` `no benefits` EQUALS 0

§§ `Goal 1 — rates and the 80% floor (ss 4A(2), 4B(2))`

#ASSERT `the rate per hour under` `eighty per cent` `, adult rate` 23.15 EQUALS 18.52
#ASSERT `the rate per hour under` (`a monetary amount per hour` 19) `, adult rate` 23.15 EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `the rate is not less than 80% of the adult rate` (`a monetary amount per hour` 18.52) 23.15
#ASSERT NOT `the rate is not less than 80% of the adult rate` (`a monetary amount per hour` 18.51) 23.15
#ASSERT NOT `the rate is not less than 80% of the adult rate` (`a percentage of the minimum adult rate` 79) 23.15

§§ `Goal 1 — the Order's power over classes (s 4A(1)-(3))`

#ASSERT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` `class A` `, adult rate` 23.15
#ASSERT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` `class B` `, adult rate` 23.15
-- a training-only class has no 6-month limit: s 4A(3) reaches factors (i) and (ii) only
#ASSERT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 19, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, 24, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
-- (1)(a): ages 16 to 19 only
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 15, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 18, 20, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
-- (1)(c): at least one factor
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
-- (1)(c)(i): "not less than 6 months" on a benefit
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 18, 19, JUST 5, JUST `any employer`, FALSE, 6, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
-- (1)(c)(ii), (3)(a)(i): "not more than 6 months" of employment
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 7, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
#ASSERT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 3, `eighty per cent`) `, adult rate` 23.15
-- (2): not less than 80%
#ASSERT NOT `the class and its rate are within s 4A` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 6, `a percentage of the minimum adult rate` 70) `, adult rate` 23.15

§§ `Goal 1 — the rate that governs (ss 4, 4A, 4B, 8(4))`

-- an adult
#ASSERT `rate for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 17, 3 months with the current employer: class A
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
-- 17, 6 months completed with the current employer: s 4A(3)(a)(i), (b) — adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 6 6 6) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 17, 2 months with this employer after 8 months elsewhere: class A counts the current employer
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 10 10 2) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
-- 17, supervising other workers: s 4A(1)(b) — adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 18, 7 months on jobseeker support, 2 months' work since: class B
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`jobseeker support for` 7) 2 2 2) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
-- 18, only 5 months on a benefit: adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`jobseeker support for` 5) 2 2 2) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 18, 7 months on a benefit, then 6 months' work with any employer: adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`jobseeker support for` 7) 6 6 1) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 18, 7 months on a benefit; worked 12 months before it, 2 since: (1)(c)(ii)(A) excludes the earlier work
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`jobseeker support for` 7) 14 2 2) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
-- 19 on a training contract, 2 years in the job: class C, no time limit
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 19 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no benefits` 24 24 24) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
-- 22 on a training contract in the Order's training class: s 4B
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 22 FALSE TRUE TRUE `no benefits` 24 24 24) EQUALS `the training rate (s 4B)` 18.52
-- 22 on a training contract, but not in a class the Order names: adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 22 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no benefits` 24 24 24) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 22 training others: s 4B(1)(b) — adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 22 TRUE TRUE TRUE `no benefits` 24 24 24) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 20: no starting-out rate (s 4A(1)(a))
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`jobseeker support for` 7) 2 2 2) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- 15: no class has a prescribed rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`worker` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3) EQUALS `no minimum rate is prescribed for the worker`
#ASSERT `the hourly minimum under` (`rate for` (`worker` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an apprentice under s 9(b)
#ASSERT `rate for` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `(b) an apprentice bound by an indenture of apprenticeship entered into under an Act`) EQUALS `the Act does not apply to the worker (ss 2, 9)`

`a permit for 2024` MEANS Permit OF 12, Date 1 1 2024, Date 31 12 2024, NOTHING

-- s 8(4): a permit in force displaces the adult rate
#ASSERT `rate for` (`with permit` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `a permit for 2024`) EQUALS `the rate stated in an exemption permit (s 8(4))` 12
-- an expired permit
#ASSERT `rate for` (`with permit` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (Permit OF 12, Date 1 1 2023, Date 31 12 2023, NOTHING)) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- a permit not yet in force (s 8(3)(a))
#ASSERT `rate for` (`with permit` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (Permit OF 12, Date 1 8 2024, Date 31 12 2024, NOTHING)) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- revoked (s 8(5))
#ASSERT `rate for` (`with permit` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (Permit OF 12, Date 1 1 2024, Date 31 12 2024, JUST (Date 1 6 2024))) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
#ASSERT `the permit is in force on` `a permit for 2024` (Date 31 12 2024)
#ASSERT NOT `the permit is in force on` (Permit OF 12, Date 1 1 2024, Date 31 12 2024, JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) (Date 1 7 2024)

-- s 4A(4): of two starting-out rates that apply, the higher
`class D` MEANS `Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, 6, `a percentage of the minimum adult rate` 90
#ASSERT `the rate that governs` (`worker` 17 FALSE TRUE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3) `under` (`Minimum Wage Order` OF 23.15, (LIST `class A`, `class D`), NOTHING) `on` `a day in 2024` EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 20.835

`an Order with a 70% class` MEANS `Minimum Wage Order` OF 23.15, (LIST (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 6, `a percentage of the minimum adult rate` 70)), NOTHING

-- an Order class below 80% that applies to the worker: the Act gives no answer
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the starting-out rate for` (`worker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3) `under` `an Order with a 70% class` `on` `a day in 2024`)
-- ... and one that does not apply to the worker is no obstacle
#ASSERT `the starting-out rate for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `under` `an Order with a 70% class` `on` `a day in 2024` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the training rate for` (`worker` 22 FALSE TRUE TRUE `no benefits` 24 24 24) `under` (`Minimum Wage Order` OF 23.15, EMPTY, JUST (`a monetary amount per hour` 15)))

§§ `Goal 2 — hours (ss 7(2), 9(e))`

`illness 4, rain 3` MEANS LIST (`Time lost` OF 4, `the worker's illness`), (`Time lost` OF 3, `another reason`)

#ASSERT `the hours the minimum applies to` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 0 `illness 4, rain 3`) EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `the hours the minimum applies to` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 0 (LIST (`Time lost` OF 2, `the default of the worker`), (`Time lost` OF 1, `an accident suffered by the worker`))) EQUALS 37
-- s 9(e): travel between clients is outside the Act for a Settlement Act employee only
#ASSERT `the hours the minimum applies to` (`in s 9 class` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `(e) an employee to whom the Home and Community Support (Payment for Travel Between Clients) Settlement Act 2016 applies`) (`period` 40 5 `no board or lodging` 0 EMPTY) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the hours the minimum applies to` (`an adult worker aged` 30) (`period` 40 5 `no board or lodging` 0 EMPTY) EQUALS 40

§§ `Goal 2 — board and lodging (s 7(1))`

`board and lodging, not fixed` MEANS `Board and lodging` OF TRUE, NOTHING, 200, TRUE, NOTHING, 20

-- 40 hours at 23.15 = 926: board up to 15% (138.90), lodging up to 5% (46.30)
#ASSERT `the most that may be deducted for board under` `board and lodging, not fixed` `from` 926 EQUALS 138.9
#ASSERT `the most that may be deducted for lodging under` `board and lodging, not fixed` `from` 926 EQUALS 46.3
-- a cash value fixed by the agreement replaces the percentage
#ASSERT `the most that may be deducted for board under` (`Board and lodging` OF TRUE, JUST 100, 0, FALSE, NOTHING, 0) `from` 926 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the most that may be deducted for lodging under` (`Board and lodging` OF TRUE, JUST 100, 0, FALSE, NOTHING, 0) `from` 926 EQUALS 0
-- 200 deducted for board counts only to 138.90; 20 for lodging counts in full
#ASSERT `the board and lodging deductions that count, under` `board and lodging, not fixed` `from` 926 EQUALS 158.9

§§ `Goal 2 — arrears (ss 6, 7, 11(1))`

-- 40 hours at 23.15 = 926; paid 900: 26 owed
#ASSERT `the arrears at` (JUST 23.15) `for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `in` (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 900 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `the arrears at` (JUST 23.15) `for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `in` (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 1000 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0
-- paid 726 in money, 200 deducted for board and 20 for lodging: 926 - 726 - 158.90 = 41.10
#ASSERT `the arrears at` (JUST 23.15) `for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `in` (`period` 40 0 `board and lodging, not fixed` 726 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 41.1
-- time lost to illness is not paid; rain is: 36 hours at 23.15 = 833.40
#ASSERT `the arrears at` (JUST 23.15) `for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `in` (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 800 `illness 4, rain 3`) EQUALS JUST 33.4
#ASSERT `the arrears at` NOTHING `for` (`an adult worker aged` 30) `in` (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 0 EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The top-level goal`

`a week for a 17-year-old` MEANS `Wage case` OF (`worker` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3), `the Order`, (`period` 30 0 `no board or lodging` 500 EMPTY)

-- 30 hours at 18.52 = 555.60; paid 500: 55.60 owed
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 17-year-old`)'s `the rate that governs` EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 17-year-old`)'s `minimum wages for the period` EQUALS JUST 555.6
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 17-year-old`)'s `arrears owed` EQUALS JUST 55.6
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 17-year-old`)'s `the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover the arrears (s 11)`

`a week for a 15-year-old` MEANS `Wage case` OF (`worker` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE `no benefits` 3 3 3), `the Order`, (`period` 30 0 `no board or lodging` 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 15-year-old`)'s `the Act applies`
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 15-year-old`)'s `arrears owed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the minimum wage position for` `a week for a 15-year-old`)'s `the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover the arrears (s 11)`

`an adult paid in full` MEANS `Wage case` OF (`an adult worker aged` 40), `the Order`, (`period` 40 0 `no board or lodging` 926 EMPTY)
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage position for` `an adult paid in full`)'s `arrears owed` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT NOT (`the minimum wage position for` `an adult paid in full`)'s `the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover the arrears (s 11)`

