§§ `Added after the independent test pass`

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, started IS A DATE
GIVETH A Worker
`a 17-year-old who started on` age started MEANS
    Worker OF TRUE, age, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `no benefits`, started, started, started, `none of the s 9 classes`, NOTHING

-- s 4A(3)(a)(i), FORK F11: first day of work 2 January 2024, so 6 months are
-- completed on 1 July 2024; the starting-out rate may be paid on that day,
-- and not the day after.
#ASSERT `the date the worker completes the employment that ends the rate` (`a 17-year-old who started on` 17 (Date 2 1 2024)) `in class` `class A` EQUALS Date 1 7 2024
#ASSERT `the rate that governs` (`a 17-year-old who started on` 17 (Date 2 1 2024)) `under` `the Order` `on` (Date 1 7 2024) EQUALS `a starting-out rate (s 4A)` 18.52
#ASSERT `the rate that governs` (`a 17-year-old who started on` 17 (Date 2 1 2024)) `under` `the Order` `on` (Date 2 7 2024) EQUALS `the adult rate (s 4)` 23.15
-- a 3-month class: first day 1 February 2024, completed on 30 April 2024
#ASSERT `the date the worker completes the employment that ends the rate` (`a 17-year-old who started on` 17 (Date 1 2 2024)) `in class` (`Starting-out class` OF 16, 17, NOTHING, JUST `the current employer`, FALSE, 3, `eighty per cent`) EQUALS Date 30 4 2024

-- s 7(1): a deduction above its ceiling breaches the Act
